"""Gera paper/s_litaudit.tex (secao do suplemento com a auditoria de literatura: rodada 1 da Entrada 159 e rodada 2 da Entrada 172, amostra agrupada) a partir de results/litaudit_pooled_entrada172.csv.
Uso: python -m analysis.make_table_litaudit
"""
from __future__ import annotations

from pathlib import Path

import numpy as np
import pandas as pd

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
inc = pd.read_csv(ROOT / "results" / "litaudit_pooled_entrada172.csv", dtype=str, keep_default_na=False)
ex1 = pd.read_csv(ROOT / "results" / "litaudit_entrada159.csv", dtype=str, keep_default_na=False)
ex2 = pd.read_csv(ROOT / "results" / "litaudit_round2_entrada172.csv", dtype=str, keep_default_na=False)
n = len(inc)
n1, n2 = int((inc["round"] == "1").sum()), int((inc["round"] == "2").sum())
nex = int((ex1.included == "N").sum()) + int((ex2.included == "N").sum())
nt = int((inc.stat_test == "Y").sum())
cnt = lambda col, v: int((inc[col] == v).sum())
claim = cnt("claim_policy_helps", "Y") + cnt("claim_policy_helps", "MIXED")
pick = sorted(np.random.default_rng(0).choice(inc.id.values, size=8, replace=False).tolist())

rows = []
for r in inc.itertuples():
    rows.append(f"arXiv:{r.id} & {r.year} & {r.random_control} & {r.budget_basis} & {r.learner_overhead_reported} & {r.offline_tuned_static} & {r.tune_test_split} & {r.stat_test} & {r.multiplicity} & {r.ablation_policy} & {r.code_or_data} & {r.claim_policy_helps} \\\\")

L = []
L.append("% Auto-generated by analysis/make_table_litaudit.py (Entradas 159 e 172)")
L.append("\\section{Audit of the literature: how often are the controls of the protocol used?}")
L.append("\\label{sec:m-litaudit}")
L.append("")
L.append(f"To check whether the controls of the protocol are common practice, {n} papers that propose a learned selector or controller of operators, strategies or parameters inside a metaheuristic for a combinatorial problem were coded, in two rounds: "
         f"{n1} papers in round 1 (eight fixed queries plus four added before reading any paper; protocol and codebook frozen before any paper was read, \\texttt{{analysis/litaudit\\_codebook\\_entrada159.md}}) and {n2} in round 2 "
         "(an amendment that changes only the sampling, \\texttt{analysis/litaudit\\_codebook\\_round2\\_entrada172.md}, frozen with a hash before any new paper was read: the same codebook, the same source and criteria, new field-qualified queries because the free-text ones returned mostly off-topic papers). "
         "The source is arXiv, 2015--2026, open full text; every exclusion ("
         f"{nex} in all) is listed with its reason in \\texttt{{results/litaudit\\_entrada159.csv}} and \\texttt{{results/litaudit\\_round2\\_entrada172.csv}}. The second round stopped at {n2} papers, below the target of $18$, because the queries were exhausted. "
         "Coding is conservative: ``U'' (cannot be determined from the text) counts as not demonstrated, and a common time limit counts as an equal-CPU budget. The sample is small, restricted to open-access arXiv papers, and coded by one coder "
         "(an AI assistant, reading the full text by retrieval with one question per item); eight papers drawn at random from the pooled sample are listed for double coding by the author "
         "(" + ", ".join(pick) + "; \\texttt{results/entrada172\\_litaudit.txt}). "
         "\\todonote{to improve: obtain papers through the institution to reach $30$ or more, and have the eight papers above double-coded by the author}")
L.append("")
L.append("\\begin{table}[t]")
L.append("\\centering")
L.append("\\caption{Coding of " + str(n) + " papers with a learned selector inside a metaheuristic (first " + str(n1) + ": round 1; last " + str(n2) + ": round 2). RC: random-selection control of the same actions; Bud: budget basis of the comparison with variants without learning (CPU: equal or common time limit; ITER: equal iterations or evaluations; MIXED; U: not stated); "
         "Ovh: cost of the learner reported or discussed; Off: static competitor tuned offline; Spl: tuning/training instances separate from test instances; Stat: statistical test; Mult: correction for multiple comparisons (NA: no test; U: tests without a stated correction); "
         "Abl: variant of the same host without the learned policy; Code: code or data available; Claim: the paper concludes that the learned component helps (Y, MIXED, N). Y: yes; N: no; U: not determinable from the text.}")
L.append("\\label{tab:litaudit}")
L.append("{\\scriptsize\\setlength{\\tabcolsep}{3pt}")
L.append("\\begin{tabular}{@{}llcccccccccc@{}}")
L.append("\\toprule")
L.append("Paper & Year & RC & Bud & Ovh & Off & Spl & Stat & Mult & Abl & Code & Claim \\\\")
L.append("\\midrule")
L += rows[:n1] + ["\\midrule"] + rows[n1:]
L.append("\\midrule")
L.append(f"Y (of {n}) & & {cnt('random_control','Y')} & {cnt('budget_basis','CPU')} & {cnt('learner_overhead_reported','Y')} & {cnt('offline_tuned_static','Y')} & {cnt('tune_test_split','Y')} & {nt} & {cnt('multiplicity','Y')}/{nt} & {cnt('ablation_policy','Y')} & {cnt('code_or_data','Y')} & {claim} \\\\")
L.append("\\bottomrule")
L.append("\\end{tabular}}")
L.append("\\end{table}")
L.append("")
L.append(f"The cheap controls are fairly common: a random-selection control in {cnt('random_control','Y')} of {n} papers and a variant of the same host without the learned policy in {cnt('ablation_policy','Y')}. "
         f"The controls that make a comparison budget-fair are rarer: only {cnt('budget_basis','CPU')} of {n} compare with the variants without learning at a common time limit ({cnt('budget_basis','ITER')} at equal iterations or evaluations, {cnt('budget_basis','MIXED')} mixed, {cnt('budget_basis','U')} not stated), "
         f"{cnt('offline_tuned_static','Y')} include a static configuration tuned offline as a competitor, {cnt('tune_test_split','Y')} state that tuning or training instances are separate from the test instances, and {cnt('multiplicity','Y')} of the {nt} that use a statistical test correct for multiple comparisons. "
         f"Of the {n} papers, {claim} conclude that the learned component helps (five of them with mixed evidence); the other one claims a different gain, that of parallelism, and none reports a null result for the policy. "
         "Predictions recorded before reading: in round 1 five of seven were wrong (random controls, ablations, overhead reports, statistical tests and multiplicity were more common than predicted; equal-CPU comparisons and offline-tuned competitors were rare, as predicted); "
         "in round 2, registered for the pooled sample, five of seven held, and the two misses are at the boundary (an equal-time-limit share of $26\\%$ against a predicted $<25\\%$, and $2$ of $10$ testers correcting for multiplicity against $<20\\%$, one of them through Tukey intervals). "
         "The pre-fixed reading of the amendment (the budget-fair controls are rare if both the equal-time-limit and the offline-tuned shares are below a third) holds ($26\\%$ and $13\\%$). "
         "The audit therefore supports the rows of Table~\\ref{tab:fair_vs_naive} that rest on equal iterations and on the absence of an offline-tuned competitor, and not a claim that random controls are uncommon.")
(ROOT / "paper" / "s_litaudit.tex").write_text("\n".join(L) + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
print("ok -> paper/s_litaudit.tex")
